menu "gpSP GBA Emulator"

    config GPSP_DYNAREC
        bool "Enable Dynamic Recompilation (Dynarec)"
        default n
        help
            Enable ARM→RISC-V dynamic recompilation for higher performance.
            Requires executable PSRAM regions. Disable this for interpreter-only mode.

    config GPSP_SMALL_TRANSLATION_CACHE
        bool "Use small translation cache"
        default y
        depends on GPSP_DYNAREC
        help
            Use smaller JIT code caches (2MB ROM / 384KB RAM instead of 10MB/512KB).
            Recommended for ESP32-P4 to conserve PSRAM.

    config GPSP_ROM_BUFFER_SIZE
        int "ROM buffer size (MB)"
        default 32
        range 1 32
        help
            Maximum ROM buffer size in megabytes.
            Allocation is graceful: if PSRAM is insufficient, fewer blocks are allocated
            and the LRU paging mechanism loads remaining pages from SD on demand.
            With 32MB PSRAM, set to 32 to cache most ROMs entirely.

    config GPSP_CPU_PROFILE_STATS
        bool "Enable CPU profile statistics"
        default n
        help
            Collect per-frame cycle counts for the CPU execution core,
            video renderer, sound mixer, and other subsystems.
            Results are printed to the log once per second.
            Adds a small overhead to every measured scope.

    config GPSP_DUAL_CORE_PPU
        bool "Dual-core PPU rendering"
        default n
        depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32P4
        help
            Offload scanline rendering (update_scanline) to a second CPU core.
            The emulation core runs ARM/Thumb CPU execution while the PPU core
            renders the previous scanline in parallel, using an IO register
            snapshot and lightweight atomic synchronization.
            Requires a dual-core ESP32-P4.

    config GPSP_P4_SIMD_PIXEL_OPS
        bool "Enable ESP32-P4 PIE pixel ops"
        default n
        depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32P4
        help
            Enable ESP32-P4 PIE (Processor Instruction Extensions) helpers for
            simple pixel-processing loops in the video renderer.

            This does not replace the GBA PPU renderer with hardware logic.
            Instead it enables selected PIE-backed helpers for simple linear
            post-processing paths such as repeated pixel fills.

            This option is experimental. It uses inline assembly with ESP32-P4
            PIE instructions and should be validated with visual testing and
            frame-time profiling on target hardware.

endmenu
